source-memory-command = Adopt selected capture as a reviewed memory note
source-memory-hint = m adopt selected capture as a memory note · approval and context selection stay explicit
source-memory-select = Choose an exact available capture in the Sources basket, then invoke remember-source or press m again. Nothing was proposed or selected.
source-memory-busy = Finish or reject the existing memory or source draft and wait for loading or saving. Your drafts were retained; no note was proposed.
source-memory-checking = Checking this exact capture against current source policy and bytes locally; no memory approval or provider request.
source-memory-unavailable = This capture or repository evidence is unavailable or excluded by current source policy. No memory was proposed.
source-memory-stale = The capture, selected basket or source bytes changed during the check. Choose and check the exact capture again; no memory was proposed.
source-memory-too-large = This capture exceeds the 4096 UTF-8 byte memory limit. It was refused without truncation.
source-memory-owner = Save the current task and keep its owner, revision, repository and Sources review unchanged while checking. No memory was proposed.
source-memory-proposed = The exact capture is now a task-scoped memory proposal in normal Memory review. Approval does not select it for context; use select-memory explicitly.
source-memory-retention = Capture/receipt/artifact purge keeps this note.
    /delete-memory removes it separately.
    Local purge is not secure erase/provider deletion.
source-memory-summary = { $scope }
    { $effect }
    Note: { $content }
    { $bytes } bytes / /verbose Full note and source
